/ActualText (Network effects are a phenomenon in which the value of a product or service increases as more people use it. This occurs because a larger user base makes the product or service more useful to everyone. For example, a social networking platform is more valuable to its users if more of their friends are on it. A messaging app is more useful if more of the people you want to communicate with are using it. And a marketplace is more attractive to buyers and sellers if it has a large number of both.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
